<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seku Wattara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1745</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sekou Ouattara</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seku Wattara was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wangara">Dyula</a> Muslim warlord who seized power in the market town of Kong, in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a>, around 1710 and founded the Kong Empire. His campaigns extended Kong's influence north towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-volta">Black Volta</a> and the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, protecting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> and Islamic learning. Members of his Wattara clan founded related states such as Gwiriko.</p></div>
